From 15c82091a2d9c4429400454478c5ac40c80f28d0 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <claude@anthropic.com>
Date: Tue, 3 Nov 2026 07:26:08 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 3/7] renderengine: Reuse blur results across frames and skip
 occluded blurs

Two output-preserving reductions in the blur path of drawLayersInternal. The
algorithm, shaders and kernels are unchanged.

Result cache. A blur whose inputs have not changed is returned from a small
cache of four entries instead of being regenerated. A static blurred surface,
such as an open notification shade, then costs no blur passes on most frames.
The key covers every input of the blur:
- the display output dataspace, max luminance and colour transform,
- for layers below: buffer identity and frame number, solid colour, opaque
  flag, dataspace and colour transform,
- for every layer: alpha, blur radius and scale, skipContentDraw, corner
  state, shadow length, transform, bounds, and blur regions.
Stacked occlusion reads the layers above, so their blur state is part of the
key. Results are stored as an owned copy, so the cache never refers to a
surface that is written again later.

To support the key, the buffer now carries its frame number, which is set
from the layer frontend for both buffer and clear paths.

Exact occlusion skip. A layer's blur is skipped when an opaque layer above it
covers its bounds completely, with the same transform, square corners, no
shadow and no colour transform, and no layer in between has a blur of its
own. The hidden blur cannot reach the output, so skipping it changes nothing.
The check is conservative: any doubt keeps the blur.

Signed-off-by: Omkar Parte <88646966+RAM-UNLOK@users.noreply.github.com>
---
