From 9fe0728fb9aeac6abd3a022e54b75fd7dbd9c05c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <claude@anthropic.com>
Date: Tue, 3 Nov 2026 09:16:07 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 6/7] renderengine: Share the KawaseDualFilterV2 downsample
 chain on preallocated targets

On the preallocated path, which is the default on device, each blur ran the
whole pipeline on the same preallocated set, including the downsample passes.

The downsample levels do not depend on the blur radius. They are now computed
once for a layer's input and reused by every blur of that layer, and each
radius runs only its upsample passes. The levels stay in the existing
preallocated set. The upsample passes write to a second preallocated set,
allocated at the same time and with the same sizes, so no pass overwrites a
level another radius still needs. Nothing is allocated during a draw.

The shared path applies only when preallocated textures are in use. The other
path, which allocates per pass, is unchanged. The arithmetic is the same as in
generateTemporaryImage, so the output is unchanged.

Signed-off-by: Omkar Parte <88646966+RAM-UNLOK@users.noreply.github.com>
---
 .../skia/filters/KawaseBlurDualFilterV2.cpp   | 159 +++++++++++++++++-
 .../skia/filters/KawaseBlurDualFilterV2.h     |  14 ++
 2 files changed, 172 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/libs/renderengine/skia/filters/KawaseBlurDualFilterV2.cpp b/libs/renderengine/skia/filters/KawaseBlurDualFilterV2.cpp
index 7be60b313d..43ee222387 100644
--- a/libs/renderengine/skia/filters/KawaseBlurDualFilterV2.cpp
+++ b/libs/renderengine/skia/filters/KawaseBlurDualFilterV2.cpp
@@ -201,6 +201,150 @@ void KawaseBlurDualFilterV2::blurInto(const sk_sp<SkSurface>& drawSurface, sk_sp
     canvas->drawPaint(paint);
